    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project" priority="binding">**PLACEMENT.** The caller-kind primitive MUST live in `src/server/shared/Spaarke.Core/Auth/` (namespace `Spaarke.Core.Auth`). NOT in BFF `Infrastructure/Auth/`, NOT inline in the endpoint. If placement in `Spaarke.Core` turns out to require a new package reference or an AspNetCore FrameworkReference, STOP and escalate rather than relocating it to the BFF.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project" priority="binding">**ONE CLASSIFIER.** After this task, exactly one place in the codebase decides caller kind from a `ClaimsPrincipal`. `AuditEnrichmentMiddleware.IsOnBehalfOfFlow` must delegate to it, not duplicate it. A second parallel claim reader fails this task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Fail closed. `Indeterminate` classification → DENY. Never infer app-only from the absence of a user claim.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">**Deny user principals outright.** A provisioning invariant diagnostic has no end-user use case. Do NOT implement "a user may ask about their own tenant" — that is the rejected option A's shape, it adds reachable surface for zero benefit, and it re-opens the enumeration oracle to every authenticated user for their own stamp. This is stricter than the ORIGINAL version of this POML prescribed; the change is deliberate.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">**An empty or absent allow-list DENIES everyone.** "Empty means allow all" is the classic failure of this pattern, and it fails open on a fresh environment where config has not been set yet.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">**The allow-list must not be satisfiable by a user-delegated token.** See `background` § THE TRAP. `appid` alone is insufficient; the check is a conjunction with a positive app-only determination.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">**Do NOT edit the L2 probe.** Option B's whole advantage over option C is that the probe is untouched — it keeps its Managed Identity and its `?tenantId=` convention. `customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1` owns that file and has an active worktree. If you find yourself needing to change it, the design has drifted — escalate.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">No new `.WithClientSecret(...)` site, and no inbound static key. The operator identity stays a Managed Identity.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">No interface for the primitive unless a second implementation genuinely exists. A static classifier or a sealed type is the expected shape.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">BFF-touching: state the Placement Justification in the PR, verify publish size ≤60 MB (baseline ~44.96 MB incl. PDBs), run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`, and add/update tests under `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/`.</constraint>
  </constraints>

